 <p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Our board of directors makes no recommendation of any kind as to the advisability of purchasing shares of common stock in the offering. </p> <p style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-weight:bold">How Columbia Financial, Inc. Intends to Use the Proceeds of the Stock Offering (page [</span>&#9679;<span style="font-weight:bold"></span><span style="font-weight:bold">]) </span></p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The following table summarizes Columbia Financial, Inc. intends to use the proceeds of the offering, based on the sale of shares at the adjusted minimum, minimum midpoint and maximum of the offering range. The table below assumes the merger consideration for the acquisition of Northfield Bancorp includes 30% cash with the remainder of the consideration in common stock of Columbia Financial, Inc. </p> <p style="font-size:12pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&#160;</p>
