<td style="vertical-align:top;text-align:left"> <p style=" margin-top:0pt ; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman;text-align:left">Includes PCD and acquired loans <span style="white-space:nowrap"><span style="white-space:nowrap">held-for-investment</span></span> (and related allowance for credit losses). </p></td></tr></table> <p style="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">At December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024, the allowance for credit losses related to PCD loans was $2.6&#160;million and $2.9&#160;million, respectively. Loans <span style="white-space:nowrap"><span style="white-space:nowrap">held-for-sale,</span></span> when applicable, are excluded from the allowance for credit losses coverage ratios in the table above. </p> <p style="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-weight:bold"><span style="font-style:italic">Allocation of Allowance for Credit Losses</span></span><span style="font-weight:bold">.</span> The following table sets forth the allowance for credit losses allocated by loan category and the percent of loans in each category to total loans at the dates indicated. The allowance for credit losses allocated to each category is not necessarily indicative of future losses in any particular category and does not restrict the use of the allowance to absorb losses in other categories. </p> <p style="font-size:12pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&#160;</p>
