<td>&#160;</td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><div style="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The Company had loans <div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;"><div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;">held-for-sale</div></div> of $<ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:LoansReceivableHeldForSaleAmount" contextRef="PAsOn12_31_2025_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_USD" decimals="-6" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170944">0</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:LoansReceivableHeldForSaleAmount" contextRef="PAsOn12_31_2024_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_USD" decimals="-5" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170945">4.9</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million at December&#160;31, 2025 and December&#160;31, 2024, respectively. </div><div style="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">In addition to originating loans, the Company may acquire loans through portfolio purchases or acquisitions of other companies. Purchased loans that have evidence of more than insignificant credit deterioration since origination are deemed PCD loans. For PCD loans, each loan pool is accounted for as a single asset with a single composite interest rate and an aggregate expectation of cash flows. PCD loans totaled $<ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableExcludingAccruedInterestBeforeAllowanceForCreditLoss" contextRef="PAsOn12_31_2025_FinancialAssetAcquiredWithCreditDeteriorationMemberusgaapCreditLossStatusAxis_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_USD" decimals="-5" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170946">8.3</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million at December&#160;31, 2025, as compared to $<ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableExcludingAccruedInterestBeforeAllowanceForCreditLoss" contextRef="PAsOn12_31_2024_FinancialAssetAcquiredWithCreditDeteriorationMemberusgaapCreditLossStatusAxis_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_USD" decimals="-5" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170947">9.2</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million at December&#160;31, 2024. The majority of the PCD loan balances were acquired as part of an FDIC-assisted transaction. At December&#160;31, 2025, PCD loans consisted of approximately <ix:nonFraction name="clbk:PercentageOfPurchaseCreditImpairedLoans" contextRef="P01_01_2025To12_31_2025_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis_OneToFourFamilyResidentialMortgageMemberusgaapFinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis" unitRef="Unit_pure" decimals="2" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170948">10</ix:nonFraction>% <div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;"><div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;">one-to-four</div></div> family residential loans, <ix:nonFraction name="clbk:PercentageOfPurchaseCreditImpairedLoans" contextRef="P01_01_2025To12_31_2025_CommercialRealEstateMemberusgaapFinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_pure" decimals="2" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170949">21</ix:nonFraction>% commercial real estate loans, <ix:nonFraction name="clbk:PercentageOfPurchaseCreditImpairedLoans" contextRef="P01_01_2025To12_31_2025_CommercialAndIndustrialLoansMemberusgaapFinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_pure" decimals="2" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170950">58</ix:nonFraction>% commercial and industrial loans, and <ix:nonFraction name="clbk:PercentageOfPurchaseCreditImpairedLoans" contextRef="P01_01_2025To12_31_2025_HomeEquityLoanMemberusgaapFinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_pure" decimals="2" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170951">11</ix:nonFraction>% in home equity loans. At December&#160;31, 2024, PCD loans consisted of approximately <ix:nonFraction name="clbk:PercentageOfPurchaseCreditImpairedLoans" contextRef="P01_01_2024To12_31_2024_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis_OneToFourFamilyResidentialMortgageMemberusgaapFinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis" unitRef="Unit_pure" decimals="2" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170952">9</ix:nonFraction>% <div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;"><div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;">one-to-four</div></div> family residential loans, <ix:nonFraction name="clbk:PercentageOfPurchaseCreditImpairedLoans" contextRef="P01_01_2024To12_31_2024_CommercialRealEstateMemberusgaapFinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_pure" decimals="2" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170953">25</ix:nonFraction>% commercial real estate loans, <ix:nonFraction name="clbk:PercentageOfPurchaseCreditImpairedLoans" contextRef="P01_01_2024To12_31_2024_CommercialAndIndustrialLoansMemberusgaapFinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_pure" decimals="2" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170954">55</ix:nonFraction>% commercial and industrial loans, and <ix:nonFraction name="clbk:PercentageOfPurchaseCreditImpairedLoans" contextRef="P01_01_2024To12_31_2024_HomeEquityLoanMemberusgaapFinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_NorthfieldBancorpIncMemberdeiLegalEntityAxis" unitRef="Unit_pure" decimals="2" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" id="ixv-170955">11</ix:nonFraction>% in home equity loans. </div><div style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><div style="text-decoration:underline;display:inline;">Credit Quality Indicators </div></div><div style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The Company monitors the credit quality of its loan portfolio on a regular basis. Credit quality is monitored by reviewing certain credit quality indicators. Management has determined that <div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;"><div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;">loan-to-value</div></div> (&#8220;LTV&#8221;) ratios (at period end) and internally assigned credit risk ratings by loan type are the key credit quality indicators that best measure the credit quality of the Company&#8217;s loan receivables. LTV ratios used by management in monitoring credit quality are based on current period loan balances and original appraised values at the time of origination (unless a current appraisal has been obtained as a result of the loan being deemed impaired). </div><div style="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The Company maintains a credit risk rating system as part of the risk assessment of its loan portfolio. The Company&#8217;s lending officers are required to assign a credit risk rating to each loan in their portfolio at origination. This risk rating is reviewed periodically and adjusted if necessary. Monthly, management presents monitored assets to the Loan Committee of the Board of Directors. In addition, the Company engages a third-party independent loan reviewer that performs semi-annual reviews of a sample of loans, validating the credit risk ratings assigned to such loans. The credit risk ratings play an important role in the establishment of the provision for credit losses on loans and the allowance for credit losses for loans <div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;"><div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;">held-for-investment.</div></div> After determining the loss factor for each portfolio segment <div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;"><div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;">held-for-investment,</div></div> the collectively evaluated for impairment balance of the <div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;"><div style="white-space:nowrap;display:inline;">held-for-investment</div></div> portfolio is multiplied by the collectively evaluated for impairment loss factor for the respective portfolio segment in order to determine the allowance for loans collectively evaluated for impairment. </div><div style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt ; font-size:8pt">&#160;</div><div style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman;text-align:center"><ix:exclude>F-99</ix:exclude> </div></ix:nonNumeric></div></div><ix:continuation id="TextSelection_156156228" continuedAt="TextSelectionAppend_156156228_1"><ix:exclude><div style="margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:0em; page-break-before:always"></div></ix:exclude></ix:continuation><ix:continuation id="TextSelectionAppend_156156228_1" continuedAt="TextSelectionAppend_156156228_2"><ix:exclude><hr style="color:#999999;height:3px;width:100%;clear:both"/></ix:exclude></ix:continuation><ix:continuation id="TextSelectionAppend_156156228_2" continuedAt="TextSelectionAppend_156156228_3"><ix:exclude><div style="font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold; margin-top: 1.67em; margin-bottom: 1.67em;"><a href="#toc">Table of Contents</a></div></ix:exclude></ix:continuation><div style="text-align:center"><div style="width:8.5in;text-align:left;margin-left: auto;margin-right: auto"><ix:continuation id="TextSelectionAppend_156156228_3" continuedAt="TextSelectionAppend_156156228_4"><ix:exclude><div style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman;font-weight:bold;text-align:center">NORTHFIELD BANCORP, INC.&#160;AND SUBSIDIARIES </div><div style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman;font-weight:bold;text-align:center">Notes to Consolidated Financial Statements&#8201;(Continued) </div><div style="font-size:12pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&#160;</div></ix:exclude></ix:continuation><ix:continuation id="TextSelectionAppend_156156228_4" continuedAt="TextSelectionAppend_156156228_5"><div style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">When assigning a credit risk rating to a loan, management utilizes the Bank&#8217;s internal nine-point credit risk rating system. </div><div style="font-size:6pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&#160;</div>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="text-align:start; BORDER-COLLAPSE:COLLAPSE; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:10pt;border-spacing:0;width:100%">
